+## Keys and roles
+
+Every request carries `Authorization: Bearer <key>`. Keys are in the data
+file as `apiKeys: [{ "key", "name", "role" }]` (`docs/DATA.md`). Without a
+key, or with a key that is not in the data, the answer is 401
+`unauthorized`; with a key whose role may not call the route it is 403
+`forbidden`.
+
+- `viewer` may call every `GET` route except `GET /audit`.
+- `cook` may also call `POST /recipes/:id/cook`, `POST /batches/:id/waste`,
+  `POST /temperatures` and `POST /stocktakes/:id/counts`.
+- `manager` may call every route.
+
+## Audit log
+
+Every request with a known key and a method other than `GET` adds an audit
+entry, whether it succeeded or not: `{ "id", "at", "keyName", "method",
+"path", "status" }`. `GET /audit` lists the entries newest first and is for
+managers only. Requests without a known key (401) are not recorded.
+
 ## Errors

 Errors have a status from `src/errors.js` and the body
